Grade marks shall be designated in a plain and conspicuous manner and be no less prominent than any trade or brand names denoting quality. (Code 1960, As Amend., § 838.100; Pet. No. 250069, § 1, 8-11-89)

As used in this chapter:

Consumer: A purchaser or lessee or prospective purchaser or lessee of goods or services. "Consumer" includes a person to whom an act or practice prohibited by this chapter is directed, although he or she is not involved in a specific transaction.

Deceptive practice: A person engages in a deceptive practice when, in the course of a business, vocation or occupation, he or she:

(a) Passes off goods or services as those of another;

(b) Causes likelihood of confusion or of misunderstanding as to the source, sponsorship, approval or certification of goods or services;

(c) Causes likelihood of confusion or of misunderstanding as to affiliation, connection or association with or certification by another;

(d) Uses deceptive representation or designations of geographic origin in connection with goods or services;

(e) Represents that goods or services have sponsorship, approval, characteristics, ingredients, uses, benefits or quantities that they do not have or that a person has a sponsorship, approval, status, affiliation or connection that he or she does not have;

(f) Represents that goods are original or new if they are deteriorated, altered, reconditioned, reclaimed, used or secondhand;

(g) Represents that goods or services are a particular standard, quality or grade or that goods are a particular style or model, if they are of another;

(h) Disparages the goods, services or business of another by false or misleading representation of fact;

(i) Advertises or offers goods or services with intent not to sell them as advertised or offered;

(j) Advertises goods or services with intent not to supply reasonably expectable public demand, unless the advertisement discloses a limitation of quantity;

(k) Makes false or misleading statements of fact concerning the reasons for, existence of, or amounts of price reductions, or price in comparison to prices of competitors or one's own price at a past or future time;

(l) Represents that a part replacement or repair service is needed when it is not;

(m) Makes false or misleading statements or representations with respect to the authority of the salesman, representative or agent to negotiate the final terms of the transaction;

(n) Makes false or misleading statements as to the legal rights, obligations or remedies of any part of the transaction.

Person: A seller or lessor who makes available goods or services to consumers. "Person" includes manufacturers, wholesalers and distributors responsible for any act or practice prohibited by this chapter. (Code 1960, As Amend., § 837.010; Pet. No. 250069, § 6, 8-11-89)

(a) Upon the request of any customer, a person engaged in the business of making repairs shall furnish to the customer a written estimate of repairs which shall state the total estimated cost of:

(1) Parts listed with reasonable particularity and identified by brand name or equivalent and designation as to whether new, rebuilt or used parts are to be installed;

(2) Labor;

(3) Incidental services;

(4) The charges, if any, for the release of the item in the event that the item is not repaired; and

(5) The charges, if any, for making the estimate.

(b) No person shall be required to prepare a written estimate of repairs for jobs under thirty-five dollars ($35.00), nor until such person has made an inspection of the item to be repaired; provided, however, that if at any time prior to or during the repair work an estimated repair cost in excess of thirty-five dollars ($35.00) is indicated, and the customer has initially requested a written estimate, an estimate in accordance with the terms and provisions of this chapter shall be required prior to continuing the repair work. The customer requesting such written estimate shall be given a signed copy of the written estimate with the word "estimate" conspicuously placed thereon, and the name and address of the business thereon. No person engaged in the business of making repairs shall solicit or demand a waiver of any customer's rights herein enumerated as a precondition to acceptance of repair work. (Code 1960, As Amend., § 840.030; Ord. of 5-30-75, § 1)

A sales certificate shall be presented by the seller to the purchaser at the time of delivery of any fuel except packaged firewood, whether it is delivered by the vendor or hauled or carried away by the purchaser. The sales certificate shall contain at the least the following information:

