In acting on an application for a permit, the Board shall consider factors which shall include, but are not limited, to the following:

(a) the public benefit to be derived from the proposed structure;

(b) the impact of the structure, both during and after construction, on soil erosion or other possible pollution of protected waters;

(c) the suitability of the floodplain or protected shoreland and the protected waters to safely accommodate the uses and traffic that the structure may generate;

(d) the impact of the structure on the views of landmarks, open spaces, vistas and protected waters; and

(e) the scale and character of the structure and its compatibility with the surrounding floodplain or protected shoreland, the protected waters and any improvements thereto. (Pk. Bd. Ord. No. 2001-102, § 1, 9-19-01)

The terms defined in PB16-2 apply to this Chapter. In addition, the terms below have the following meanings:

Crimes against a person means Criminal Homicide, Forcible Rape, Robbery and Aggravated Assault.

Neighborhood means that section of the City defined by the bylaws of the relevant neighborhood organization required by the Neighborhood Revitalization Program Law, Minn. Stat. § 469.1831, subd. 6(b), and reference by City of Minneapolis Geographic Information Systems map Neighborhoods &amp; Communities.

Park staff means any employee of the Minneapolis Park and Recreation Board.

Superintendent means the Superintendent of the Minneapolis Park and Recreation Board. (Pk. Bd. Ord. No. 2016-102 , § 1, 7-6-16)

Undeveloped Park means any park owned, leased, or operated by MPRB, with the exception of properties acquired for the purpose of preserving an existing community garden as permitted under the Community Gardens Policy, that has none of the following six asset types:

●Buildings open to the public at regular times;

●Permanent open-air shelters meant for picnicking, gathering, or performances;

●Athletic fields, whether with permanent vertical infrastructure or simply lawn areas that are occasionally programmed;

●Courts, including hard surfaced, sand, aggregate, or turf, provided that a turf court has a vertical element to facilitate play;

●Aquatic facilities; or

●Designated play areas, either with manufactured play equipment or with nature-play elements.

(Pk. Bd. Ord. No. 2016-102, § 1, 7-6-16; Ord. No. 2023-101, § 1, 9-20-23)

The human resources department shall establish, implement, and oversee merit based procedures for assessing applicants and filling vacancies in the classified service. The procedures shall be based on sound human resources principles that:

(1) Support the values and goals of the Minneapolis Park and Recreation;

(2) Are based on bona fide job qualifications;

(3) Seek to eliminate personal and/or institutional bias in hiring decisions;

(4) Include measures that promote continuous improvement in the hiring process; and

(5) Result in an eligibility register consisting of a pool of qualified applicants. (Pk. Bd. Ord. No. 2017-102, § 1, 10-4-17)
